00:03:13.960 --> 00:03:17.700
- So in reality, before you
even get close to a courtroom

00:03:17.700 --> 00:03:19.890
you're going to go through
a process called discovery.

00:03:19.890 --> 00:03:21.720
Discovery is the process by which you

00:03:21.720 --> 00:03:23.730
get information from the other side

00:03:23.730 --> 00:03:25.580
and the other side gets
information from you.

00:03:25.580 --> 00:03:28.580
You are allowed to request
relevant documents.

00:03:28.580 --> 00:03:30.760
You're allowed to ask
the other side questions.

00:03:30.760 --> 00:03:33.400
And you are allowed to
question them in person

00:03:33.400 --> 00:03:35.370
under oath through depositions.

00:03:35.370 --> 00:03:38.160
So, before you ever get
close to a courtroom

00:03:38.160 --> 00:03:39.480
you're going to have to interact

00:03:39.480 --> 00:03:41.290
with the other side
whether you want to or not.

00:03:41.290 --> 00:03:43.340
Many, many times through discovery

00:03:43.340 --> 00:03:45.760
there is no longer any
trial by sandbagging.

00:03:45.760 --> 00:03:47.590
You have to turn over relevant information

00:03:47.590 --> 00:03:49.220
to the other side and the other side

00:03:49.220 --> 00:03:51.270
has to turn over relevant
information to you.

00:03:51.270 --> 00:03:53.290
So, you would never
just introduce yourself

00:03:53.290 --> 00:03:55.260
for the first time at trial.

00:03:55.260 --> 00:03:57.860
This episode appears
to have skipped through

00:03:57.860 --> 00:04:01.210
