00:06:00.810 --> 00:06:03.400
- You're not allowed to
bring in character evidence

00:06:03.400 --> 00:06:05.700
except under very specific circumstances,

00:06:05.700 --> 00:06:07.430
none of which are present here.

00:06:07.430 --> 00:06:09.050
Character evidence is where you're saying

00:06:09.050 --> 00:06:11.390
that someone has a certain
character for acting

00:06:11.390 --> 00:06:13.490
in a certain way and therefore,

00:06:13.490 --> 00:06:16.730
they likely acted in that
way that is in conformity

00:06:16.730 --> 00:06:19.280
with their character
on a specific instance.

00:06:19.280 --> 00:06:21.650
Courts, I think rightfully, look down

00:06:21.650 --> 00:06:25.040
on that kind of tenuous specious argument,

00:06:25.040 --> 00:06:26.720
and they don't allow that to come

00:06:26.720 --> 00:06:29.000
in except under very rare circumstances.

00:06:29.000 --> 00:06:30.830
And additionally, in an opening statement,

00:06:30.830 --> 00:06:32.440
you are not supposed to be arguing,

00:06:32.440 --> 00:06:34.350
which is what this attorney is doing.

00:06:34.350 --> 00:06:37.480
So, despite claiming to
be a very good lawyer,

00:06:37.480 --> 00:06:39.660
he's not doing a great job so far.

00:06:39.660 --> 00:06:41.600
It looks like he's
allowing his personal bias

00:06:41.600 --> 00:06:43.763
to enter into his opening statement.

00:06:44.750 --> 00:06:47.600
- Your Honor, I'll keep it brief.

00:06:47.600 --> 00:06:49.523
