from seeing some of those.

00:10:05.900 --> 00:10:08.010
- You know, I feel like I'm
not being utilized properly.

00:10:08.010 --> 00:10:09.110
- Well that's cause you
don't have anything,

00:10:09.110 --> 00:10:10.740
so you're not being utilized at all.

00:10:10.740 --> 00:10:12.890
- Yeah but what if I get
to deliver the bomb shell?

00:10:12.890 --> 00:10:13.723
- Ohh.

00:10:14.590 --> 00:10:16.230
- What bomb shell?

00:10:16.230 --> 00:10:17.740
- You guys don't have a bomb shell?

00:10:17.740 --> 00:10:20.580
Oh my god, every good
case needs a bomb shell.

00:10:20.580 --> 00:10:22.720
Oh Jesus Christ, without
it, you're screwed.

00:10:22.720 --> 00:10:23.561
- Okay.

00:10:23.561 --> 00:10:25.380
- You know what, you know
what, I'll find one for ya.

00:10:25.380 --> 00:10:27.890
I'm gonna do like a hero
cop Mark Fuhrman thing.

00:10:27.890 --> 00:10:29.520
And then sort of transition
and do a caito calen.

00:10:29.520 --> 00:10:30.740
- Yeah, I wish you would do none of it.

00:10:30.740 --> 00:10:32.500
I wish you'd do none of it, man.

00:10:32.500 --> 00:10:35.380
- In reality, cases
rarely have bomb shells.

00:10:35.380 --> 00:10:36.850
That's the whole point of discovery,

00:10:36.850 --> 00:10:39.120
is not to be able to
sandbag the other side

00:10:39.120 --> 00:10:42.510
or to pull out some crazy theory, or fact

00:10:42.510 --> 00:10:43.810
in the middle of trial.

00:10:43.810 --> 00:10:46.160
In reality, you want the case to end

00:10:46.160 --> 00:10:48.260
as soon as possible, whether
that's through settlement,

00:10:48.260 --> 00:10:50.500
or through trial, or through dismissal.

00:10:50.500 --> 00:10:52.970
So you don't want things
to wait until the end,

00:10:52.970 --> 00:10:55.330
and in real life, you
don't have bomb shells.

00:10:55.330 --> 00:10:58.160
Those are disposed of a long, long time

00:10:58.160 --> 00:10:59.590
before you ever get to court.

00:10:59.590 --> 00:11:03.190
- Your honor, nothing
represents the tragic aftermath

00:11:03.190 --> 00:11:07.030
more than the dramatic
transformation of this woman.

00:11:07.030 --> 00:11:08.090
- Cat.

00:11:08.090 --> 00:11:08.923
- Excuse me?

00:11:08.923 --> 00:11:10.530
- As I transition from woman to cat,

00:11:10.530 --> 00:11:12.923
I must insist on being
referred to as a cat.

00:11:14.320 --> 00:11:16.737
- Objection, she's not a cat, your honor.

00:11:16.737 --> 00:11:17.570
(Maureen hisses)

00:11:17.570 --> 00:11:18.888
- Also what is the
relevance of this testimony?

00:11:18.888 --> 00:11:19.721
- If the witness wants to consider

00:11:19.721 --> 00:11:21.450
herself a cat, I will allow it.

00:11:21.450 --> 00:11:23.670
I just need to know
where all this is headed.

00:11:23.670 --> 00:11:24.570
How is this relevant?

00:11:24.570 --> 00:11:25.403
- Well it's--

00:11:25.403 --> 00:11:26.368
- Thank you.

00:11:26.368 --> 00:11:28.810
- Clearly relevant the attack
had a psychological impact

00:11:28.810 --> 00:11:32.083
on all the parties that
evening, no further questions.

00:11:33.930 --> 00:11:36.180
- Okay first of all, that has no relevance

00:11:36.180 --> 00:11:39.030
as to whether the person did the thing

00:11:39.030 --> 00:11:40.340
that they were accused of, which I guess

00:11:40.340 --> 00:11:43.780
is spiking some milk with bath salts.

00:11:43.780 --> 00:11:46.980
And number two, they're not
suing for psychological damages,

00:11:46.980 --> 00:11:50.390
so all of this testimony,
whatever psychological effect

00:11:50.390 --> 00:11:53.180
it had on other people, has
no bearing on this case.

00:11:53.180 --> 00:11:56.660
And whether it injured other
people who are not plaintiffs

00:11:56.660 --> 00:12:00.060
here, again, not relevant
to this particular case.

00:12:00.060 --> 00:12:02.230
So, all of this is irrelevant.

00:12:02.230 --> 00:12:04.693
- Your honor, do you see
what's going on here?

00:12:04.693 --> 00:12:07.770
This is crazy, you know what,
I'm gonna approach the bench.

00:12:07.770 --> 00:12:08.603
- No!

00:12:08.603 --> 00:12:09.770
- Can I just approach it real fast?

00:12:09.770 --> 00:12:10.880
- Absolutely not.

00:12:10.880 --> 00:12:13.280
- Alright, earlier you
referred to my ex-wife

00:12:13.280 --> 00:12:15.340
as a cat, per her request, now surely

00:12:15.340 --> 00:12:18.890
you wouldn't force a man to
pay alimony to a cat, right?

00:12:18.890 --> 00:12:21.410
So motion to establish me
having to pay alimony anymore.

00:12:21.410 --> 00:12:22.600
- I will not allow that.

00:12:22.600 --> 00:12:25.420
- Okay, well so, can we just,
we'll pop it on the docket?

00:12:25.420 --> 00:12:26.620
We can put it at the end
of the day, if you want.

00:12:26.620 --> 00:12:28.380
I just want to clear it up
while I got her in a courtroom.

00:12:28.380 --> 00:12:30.733
- I will not allow that either, sit down.

00:12:31.580 --> 00:12:34.990
- Alright, I mean, that was
probably the right result here.

00:12:34.990 --> 00:12:37.890
There's no reason why he
should have this matter heard

00:12:37.890 --> 00:12:39.760
in front of this judge in this court.

00:12:39.760 --> 00:12:42.170
None of that is related to family law.

00:12:42.170 --> 00:12:44.050
I probably don't need to tell you that

00:12:44.050 --> 00:12:45.840
people in the gallery are not allowed

00:12:45.840 --> 00:12:49.400
to make legal arguments or
request relief from the court.

00:12:49.400 --> 00:12:50.337
- He totally did it.

00:12:50.337 --> 00:12:51.702
(audience whispering)

00:12:51.702 --> 00:12:53.950
- Okay, well, then I
guess we will never know,

00:12:53.950 --> 00:12:54.880
ladies and gentleman.

00:12:54.880 --> 00:12:56.490
- Uncle Jack, he just confessed!

00:12:56.490 --> 00:12:57.323
- He did?

00:12:57.323 --> 00:12:58.660
- Yes!

00:12:58.660 --> 00:13:00.410
- Yeah, Ryan stabbed
Liam, I totally saw it.

00:13:00.410 --> 00:13:02.192
- Oh my god, we won!

00:13:02.192 --> 00:13:05.410
(audience cheering)

00:13:05.410 --> 00:13:08.090
- So you see this a lot in
legal movies and TV shows.

00:13:08.090 --> 00:13:09.780
There will be one good piece of evidence

00:13:09.780 --> 00:13:11.270
that comes out on the
stand, and then suddenly

00:13:11.270 --> 00:13:15.030
everyone is celebrating as if
they have won the court case.

00:13:15.030 --> 00:13:16.620
This is not the end of the game,

00:13:16.620 --> 00:13:17.940
this is just the very beginning.

00:13:17.940 --> 00:13:19.790
There will be lots of other testimony,

00:13:19.790 --> 00:13:22.210
and rarely is one fact dispositive,

00:13:22.210 --> 00:13:25.100
and certainly not this particular fact.

00:13:25.100 --> 00:13:27.680
- Lyon, was Ryan drinking
milk at the wedding?

00:13:27.680 --> 00:13:29.470
- Of course, everyone was.

00:13:29.470 --> 00:13:32.840
- So, who did the stabbing
doesn't matter, your honor.

00:13:32.840 --> 00:13:36.730
Because they were all still
drugged on Bill Ponderosa's

00:13:36.730 --> 00:13:39.710
spiked milk, which is the
point I've been trying to make

00:13:39.710 --> 00:13:42.380
the entire time, so just to be clear,

00:13:42.380 --> 00:13:45.808
you've proven my case, you lose.

00:13:45.808 --> 00:13:48.140
(audience groans)

00:13:48.140 --> 00:13:50.320
- Okay, a couple of things, number one,

00:13:50.320 --> 00:13:51.780
you're not allowed to make argument

00:13:51.780 --> 00:13:54.400
in the middle of a cross examination.

00:13:54.400 --> 00:13:56.530
This happens in movies and TV shows

00:13:56.530 --> 00:13:58.140
but it is not realistic at all,

00:13:58.140 --> 00:13:59.620
you are allowed to ask questions,

00:13:59.620 --> 00:14:03.210
you are allowed to receive
the answer from the witnesses.

00:14:03.210 --> 00:14:05.810
But you are not allowed
to just turn around

00:14:05.810 --> 00:14:08.780
and start talking to the judge
and talking to the other side

00:14:08.780 --> 00:14:10.627
and arguing your case.

00:14:10.627 --> 00:14:12.000
(intense music)

00:14:12.000 --> 00:14:14.610
- Okay, Mr.McDonald,
you recently found out

00:14:14.610 --> 00:14:16.680
some very interesting information,

00:14:16.680 --> 00:14:18.600
care to share it with the court?

00:14:18.600 --> 00:14:21.450
- Yes, I've recently been informed that

00:14:21.450 --> 00:14:25.168
Ryan McPoyle only drinks Mother's milk.

00:14:25.168 --> 00:14:26.001
(audience gasps)

00:14:26.001 --> 00:14:29.290
Which means, there's no way
he could've drank the milk

00:14:29.290 --> 00:14:31.900
that Bill spiked, which means he was sober

00:14:31.900 --> 00:14:33.730
when he attacked his brother, which means

00:14:33.730 --> 00:14:38.523
Bill is innocent, case
closed, kaboom, bomb shell!

00:14:39.990 --> 00:14:43.650
- Alright just as an
attorney is not allowed

00:14:43.650 --> 00:14:46.310
to make argument during
a cross examination,

00:14:46.310 --> 00:14:49.650
neither can the witness
go off and make argument.

00:14:49.650 --> 00:14:53.390
If he has evidence, great,
state your testimony, state the

00:14:53.390 --> 00:14:56.550
percipient facts that you
personally have witnessed.

00:14:56.550 --> 00:14:59.200
But you can't then just go on this tirade

00:14:59.200 --> 00:15:01.730
making argument about what you can infer

00:15:01.730 --> 00:15:04.000
from the different kinds of evidence.

00:15:04.000 --> 00:15:06.090
So, everybody's making argument here,

00:15:06.090 --> 00:15:09.470
it's very entertaining, it
is not realistic at all.

00:15:09.470 --> 00:15:11.380
- How did you come upon this information?

00:15:11.380 --> 00:15:13.210
- Oh I banged Margaret McPoyle.

00:15:13.210 --> 00:15:17.310
- I'm curious how she told you
because Margaret is a mute.

00:15:17.310 --> 00:15:18.740
- It's still hearsay either way.

00:15:18.740 --> 00:15:20.040
- I had her write it down.

00:15:21.370 --> 00:15:23.420
- Alright, just because
she has written this down,

00:15:23.420 --> 00:15:25.220
does not make it any less hearsay,

00:15:25.220 --> 00:15:26.760
it is still an out of court statement

00:15:26.760 --> 00:15:29.040
used for the truth of the matter asserted

00:15:29.040 --> 00:15:34.010
that only Mother's milk is
consumed by the individual.

00:15:34.010 --> 00:15:36.370
Oh boy, this is so weird.

00:15:36.370 --> 00:15:40.430
- Your honor, Mother is the
name of the McPoyle family cow.

00:15:40.430 --> 00:15:42.470
The cow that provided
the milk for the wedding,

00:15:42.470 --> 00:15:47.460
the milk that was drugged
by Bill Ponderosa.

00:15:47.460 --> 00:15:48.293
- That mute--

00:15:48.293 --> 00:15:49.126
(bleeping sound)

00:15:49.126 --> 00:15:51.040
lied to me, for sex!

00:15:51.040 --> 00:15:52.895
- Bomb shell diffused.

00:15:52.895 --> 00:15:54.690
- Abrahmowitz!

00:15:54.690 --> 00:15:57.627
- Alright so there are
a lot of problems here.

00:15:57.627 --> 00:16:00.620
The lawyer is again making argument

00:16:00.620 --> 00:16:02.890
without getting testimony
from the witness.

00:16:02.890 --> 00:16:05.310
You need to save your argument
for the closing argument.

00:16:05.310 --> 00:16:08.730
He's getting testimony from
someone sitting in the gallery.

00:16:08.730 --> 00:16:11.890
Just call her to the
stand, you can have a deaf

00:16:11.890 --> 00:16:14.700
or mute person testify
through an interpreter.

00:16:14.700 --> 00:16:16.760
That's a very easy thing to do.

00:16:16.760 --> 00:16:19.940
And, you have to enter this
picture that is being discussed

00:16:19.940 --> 00:16:23.880
into evidence, otherwise
none of this counts at all.

00:16:23.880 --> 00:16:26.560
- This is the McPoyle family crest.

00:16:26.560 --> 00:16:28.610
On it you will find a bird,

00:16:28.610 --> 00:16:30.710
a Pocono Swallow, to be more accurate.

00:16:30.710 --> 00:16:32.840
A very rare, very elusive bird.

00:16:32.840 --> 00:16:34.670
You'll notice its trademark unibrow,

00:16:34.670 --> 00:16:37.170
highly uncommon in most aviary circles.

00:16:37.170 --> 00:16:39.790
And my research shows
that unlike your typical

00:16:39.790 --> 00:16:42.910
North American barn
swallow, the Pocono Swallow,

00:16:42.910 --> 00:16:44.492
if kept under the proper conditions--

00:16:44.492 --> 00:16:45.797
- What does this have to do with anything?

00:16:45.797 --> 00:16:49.270
- 80 to even 85 years, much like a parrot,

00:16:49.270 --> 00:16:52.140
or some of the more
resilient coastal gulls.

00:16:52.140 --> 00:16:54.680
- Your honor, where is this going?

00:16:54.680 --> 00:16:57.910
- I don't know, but it
better lead somewhere fast.

00:16:57.910 --> 00:16:58.743
- He's gonna say I"ll allow it.

00:16:58.743 --> 00:16:59.576
- Your honor, I can assure you

00:16:59.576 --> 00:17:01.140
that this will be our final argument.

00:17:01.140 --> 00:17:02.130
- Well if it's gonna help end

00:17:02.130 --> 00:17:04.210
all of this madness, I'll allow it.

00:17:04.210 --> 00:17:05.423
- I'll allow it!

00:17:05.423 --> 00:17:06.480
(he laughs)

00:17:06.480 --> 00:17:10.290
Again, you're not allowed to
just bring in random posters

00:17:10.290 --> 00:17:13.053
into evidence, you're not
allowed to make argument,

00:17:13.910 --> 00:17:16.450
whether should be some testimony going on.

00:17:16.450 --> 00:17:18.130
Charlie has said that this will

00:17:18.130 --> 00:17:19.617
constitute their final argument.

00:17:19.617 --> 00:17:22.440
But the problem is, 100% of
what he is talking about,

00:17:22.440 --> 00:17:25.170
never came out in court, so all of this

00:17:25.170 --> 00:17:27.380
is not in evidence, you're
not allowed to make argument

00:17:27.380 --> 00:17:31.120
based on facts that did not
come out in the trial itself.

00:17:31.120 --> 00:17:34.050
So all of this is improper,
whether this is in place

00:17:34.050 --> 00:17:36.910
of testimony, or whether
it's in place of argument.

00:17:36.910 --> 00:17:40.140
It's all ridiculous, it
doesn't seem relevant at all,

00:17:40.140 --> 00:17:42.690
and it's 100% improper.

00:17:42.690 --> 00:17:45.210
- Bye bye birdie.

00:17:45.210 --> 00:17:46.873
Ready boys and girls, because
here where it gets good.

00:17:46.873 --> 00:17:50.520
Ryan McPoyle didn't
attack Liam, Royal did.

00:17:50.520 --> 00:17:53.220
And Lyon was lying about
Ryan attaching Liam

00:17:53.220 --> 00:17:56.030
to protect Royal from the
chair, or lethal injection,

00:17:56.030 --> 00:17:58.400
or perhaps some sort of
small bird guillotine.

00:17:58.400 --> 00:17:59.880
I wouldn't understand the physics of it,

00:17:59.880 --> 00:18:02.250
I'm not an executioner, I'm just the best

00:18:02.250 --> 00:18:04.143
God damn bird lawyer in the world.

00:18:06.580 --> 00:18:08.160
- Okay, I guess that could be true.

00:18:08.160 --> 00:18:10.620
He could be the best
bird lawyer in the world.

00:18:10.620 --> 00:18:13.240
That's not really a thing, but he is

00:18:13.240 --> 00:18:15.820
one of the worst trial
lawyers I have ever seen.

00:18:15.820 --> 00:18:18.380
He does nothing but improperly argue at

00:18:18.380 --> 00:18:21.250
times when he should
be eliciting evidence.

00:18:21.250 --> 00:18:25.110
He is relying on speculation,
on facts not on the record.

00:18:25.110 --> 00:18:28.420
On hearsay, on irrelevant testimony.

00:18:28.420 --> 00:18:31.010
He tried to get evidence
out of the gallery,

00:18:31.010 --> 00:18:33.930
he tried to bring in new
evidence that hasn't come out

00:18:33.930 --> 00:18:35.730
during his closing arguments.

00:18:35.730 --> 00:18:39.110
He's basically breaking
every rule that exists

00:18:39.110 --> 00:18:41.730
in civil procedure at this time.

00:18:41.730 --> 00:18:44.040
This is the biggest train wreck of a trial

00:18:44.040 --> 00:18:45.700
I have ever seen in my entire life.

00:18:45.700 --> 00:18:48.570
And I have seen a lot
of trials, this is bad.

00:18:48.570 --> 00:18:50.870
- So bottom line, and listen up numb nuts

00:18:50.870 --> 00:18:55.313
cause it blows a whole in your
case, birds don't drink milk.

00:18:56.430 --> 00:18:59.220
- Facts not in evidence, improper opinion.

00:18:59.220 --> 00:19:02.483
- Didn't the bailiff ask
everyone to remove their hats?

00:19:03.700 --> 00:19:05.447
- That is true, Mr. McPoyle,

00:19:07.134 --> 00:19:08.948
would you please remover your hat?

00:19:08.948 --> 00:19:09.781
(McPoyle makes grunting sound)

00:19:09.781 --> 00:19:12.320
Mr. McPoyle, please remove your hat.

00:19:12.320 --> 00:19:15.120
- Perhaps he is too insane
to understand the question.

00:19:15.120 --> 00:19:17.143
Why don't I just ...

00:19:18.959 --> 00:19:19.792
(bird squawking)

00:19:19.792 --> 00:19:20.950
(audience gasping)

00:19:20.950 --> 00:19:23.340
- So as ridiculous as this part is,

00:19:23.340 --> 00:19:25.730
there is actually a part of
the Code of Civil Procedure

00:19:25.730 --> 00:19:28.300
that does allow for a physical inspection

00:19:28.300 --> 00:19:29.900
of the other side, you
have to make a motion

00:19:29.900 --> 00:19:31.760
with the court and there
are certain hurdles

00:19:31.760 --> 00:19:33.440
that you have to go through,
because you can imagine

00:19:33.440 --> 00:19:37.960
that people could abuse the
right to physically inspect

00:19:37.960 --> 00:19:39.310
the other side or to ask the

00:19:39.310 --> 00:19:42.520
other side to get a medical examination.

00:19:42.520 --> 00:19:45.280
But there are actual
provisions of the code

00:19:45.280 --> 00:19:47.720
that allow you to do
that when it is relevant

00:19:47.720 --> 00:19:50.220
to the specific case, who knew?

00:19:50.220 --> 00:19:52.270
- Your honor, this is Mr. Belka Maier.

00:19:52.270 --> 00:19:53.610
He's the professor of ornithology

00:19:53.610 --> 00:19:55.120
at the University of Penn.

00:19:55.120 --> 00:19:56.740
Mr. Maier, it's safe to say you're

00:19:56.740 --> 00:19:58.240
a bit of an expert on birds, yes?

00:19:58.240 --> 00:19:59.276
- I believe you're correct.

00:19:59.276 --> 00:20:00.109
- And you would understand this

00:20:00.109 --> 00:20:01.567
Pocono Swallow quite well, wouldn't you?

00:20:01.567 --> 00:20:02.490
- Yes I do.

00:20:02.490 --> 00:20:05.100
- Then please ask it if it attacked Liam.

00:20:05.100 --> 00:20:06.980
- Okay, I probably don't
need to tell you this,

00:20:06.980 --> 00:20:08.640
but you are not allowed to conduct

00:20:08.640 --> 00:20:11.360
a second examination
of a different witness,

00:20:11.360 --> 00:20:14.500
while you have a first
witness on the stand,

00:20:14.500 --> 00:20:17.000
in the first place, you just
have to excuse the first one

00:20:17.000 --> 00:20:19.150
then call the other person
back up to the stand.

00:20:19.150 --> 00:20:22.480
If you need to readdress
issues with the first witness,

00:20:22.480 --> 00:20:24.350
you can call them again
as a rebuttal witness.

00:20:24.350 --> 00:20:28.100
Or ask for a redirect,
but you're not allowed

00:20:28.100 --> 00:20:30.140
to have someone sit at counsel table

00:20:30.140 --> 00:20:33.120
and ask them separate questions,
he's not even under oath.

00:20:33.120 --> 00:20:35.353
This is all very, very improper.

00:20:36.360 --> 00:20:38.230
- In my 35 years on this bench,

00:20:38.230 --> 00:20:41.120
I have never seen such a
mockery made of this courtroom.

00:20:41.120 --> 00:20:44.270
You people have wasted my time,

00:20:44.270 --> 00:20:46.200
you've wasted the taxpayer's time,

00:20:46.200 --> 00:20:49.262
and this justice has heard enough.

00:20:49.262 --> 00:20:50.095
- Finally.

00:20:50.095 --> 00:20:50.928
- I am throwing this case out.

00:20:50.928 --> 00:20:52.140
I should've done it hours ago.

00:20:52.140 --> 00:20:53.940
- Yes you should've thrown out this case,

00:20:53.940 --> 00:20:55.740
it was ridiculous.

00:20:55.740 --> 00:20:59.360
- This court has ruled, now I suggest

00:20:59.360 --> 00:21:01.820
that you people get the
hell out of my courtroom

00:21:01.820 --> 00:21:03.270
before I put you all in jail.

00:21:03.270 --> 00:21:06.331
- Yep, rule number one,
never piss off the judge.

00:21:06.331 --> 00:21:08.914
(upbeat music)

00:21:11.010 --> 00:21:14.590
Okay, now it's time to give
McPoyle versus Ponderosa

00:21:14.590 --> 00:21:16.605
a grade for legal realism.

00:21:16.605 --> 00:21:19.090
(gavel banging)

00:21:19.090 --> 00:21:20.890
So they didn't get a whole lot right.

00:21:20.890 --> 00:21:24.780
They had counsel tables, and
wood panels on the walls.

00:21:24.780 --> 00:21:27.000
On the other hand, you have
lawyers making argument

00:21:27.000 --> 00:21:29.840
instead of asking questions,
you have neither side

00:21:29.840 --> 00:21:32.400
really getting any evidence
out, you have facts

00:21:32.400 --> 00:21:34.540
that were never mentioned at any point.

00:21:34.540 --> 00:21:36.940
So they basically get everything wrong.

00:21:36.940 --> 00:21:39.990
Now I've never done this,
but I think this episode

00:21:39.990 --> 00:21:41.950
of It's Always Sunny in Philadelphia

00:21:41.950 --> 00:21:46.950
deserves a flat F, I would
not allow this in my court.

00:21:47.630 --> 00:21:48.463
Do you agree?

00:21:48.463 --> 00:21:50.130
Leave your objections down below,

00:21:50.130 --> 00:21:52.110
and check out my other reactions over here

00:21:52.110 --> 00:21:54.993
where as always I will see you in court.

